#PBS -S /bin/bash
#PBS -N enkfgdas_fcst_%CYC%_mem%ENSMEM%
#PBS -j oe
#PBS -q %QUEUE%
#PBS -A %PROJ%-%PROJENVIR%
#PBS -l walltime=00:30:00
#PBS -l select=8:mpiprocs=128:ompthreads=1:ncpus=128
#PBS -l place=vscatter:exclhost
#PBS -l debug=true

model=gfs
export cyc="%CYC%"
%include <head.h>
%include <envir-p1.h>

############################################################
# Load modules
############################################################
#TODO: load only the modules needed for each job
source ${HOMEgfs}/dev/ush/load_modules.sh ufswm

module list
############################################################
# CALL executable job script here
############################################################
export HOMEglobal=${HOMEgfs}
export WGF="%WGF%"
export ENSMEM="%ENSMEM%"
export MEMDIR="%MEMDIR%"

#### ${HOMEgfs}/dev/job_cards/rocoto/fcst.sh
${HOMEgfs}/jobs/JGLOBAL_FORECAST
if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then
   ecflow_client --msg="***JOB ${ECF_NAME} ERROR RUNNING J-SCRIPT ***"
   ecflow_client --abort
   exit
fi

%include <tail.h>
%manual

TASK enkfgdas_fcst_master

PURPOSE: EnKF ensemble member forecast -- runs 9-hour coupled UFS for a single
ensemble member. 8 nodes per member. Per-member _master template (80
members).

TROUBLESHOOTING

Same UFS model as deterministic but lower resolution and without wave coupling. 
If a single member or a few members fail, the recovery strategy 
is to copy the entire contents of a successful member from COM 
(ie. enkfgdas.${PDY}/${CYC}/mem${MEM}/*) to the failed member. 
If all enkf forecast members fail,  it is possible that upstream analysis 
might be the cause, but we can also look to decrease the model 
forecast time steps. 
To  reduce the atm time step, in the GFSv17 package, in 
parm/gfs/config.ufs change DELTIM=300 in the ${fv3_res}=C384 
section without a nest, to DELTIM=150. 
To reduce the ocn time step, in the GFSv17 package, in 
parm/gfs/config.ufs in the "MOM6 specific settings" section for case 
${mom6_res}=025 change, OCNTIM='900' and
 DT_THERM_MOM6='1800' -> '900'. 
Note this section is used for gfs and gdas forecasts as well and will 
need to be changed back for those forecasts to run with the original 
time steps.

%end
